.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt ACZ 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm acz ,
.Nm unacz ,
.Nm aczcat
.Nd compress and decompress files with an adaptive arithmetic coder
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm acz
.Op Fl cdfkqtvz
.Op Fl 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4
.Op Fl T Ar threads
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl -block Ns = Ns Ar size
.Op Fl -dedup Ns Op = Ns Ar size
.Op Fl -memory Ns = Ns Ar size
.Op Fl -rm
.Op Ar
.Nm unacz
.Op Ar option ...
.Op Ar
.Nm aczcat
.Op Ar option ...
.Op Ar
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
compresses each
.Ar file
into
.Ar file Ns Pa .acz
with an adaptive model and an arithmetic coder.
.Nm unacz
is
.Nm
.Fl d ,
and
.Nm aczcat
is
.Nm
.Fl dc .
With no
.Ar file ,
or when
.Ar file
is
.Sq - ,
they read standard input and write standard output.
.Pp
Input files are kept unless
.Fl -rm
is given.
An existing output is not replaced unless
.Fl f
is given.
Compressed data is neither written to nor read from a terminal unless
.Fl f
is given.
.Pp
The input is coded in independent blocks, on as many threads as the
memory limit allows.
The output does not depend on the number of threads.
Decompression needs no options: the model, the block size and the
long-repeat window are read from the stream.
Concatenated
.Pa .acz
streams decompress to the concatenation of their contents.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl z , Fl -compress
Compress.
This is the default for
.Nm .
.It Fl d , Fl -decompress , Fl -uncompress
Decompress.
This is the default for
.Nm unacz
and
.Nm aczcat .
.It Fl t , Fl -test
Check the integrity of compressed files and write nothing.
.It Fl c , Fl -stdout , Fl -to-stdout
Write to standard output and keep the input files.
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -output Ns = Ns Ar file
Write all output to
.Ar file .
Several inputs make one stream of several members.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace existing outputs, and allow compressed data on a terminal.
.It Fl k , Fl -keep
Keep the input files.
This is the default.
.It Fl -rm
Remove each input file once its output is complete.
.It Fl 0 , 1 , 2 , 3 , 4 ; Fl -order Ns = Ns Ar n
Choose the model.
The default is
.Fl 4 .
.Bl -tag -width 2n -compact
.It Cm 0
Byte frequencies alone.
.It Cm 1
The previous byte.
.It Cm 2
The previous two bytes, a bit at a time.
.It Cm 3
Prediction by partial matching, with contexts of up to six bytes.
.It Cm 4
Context mixing, which compresses best and takes longest.
.El
.It Fl T Ar n , Fl -threads Ns = Ns Ar n
Use at most
.Ar n
worker threads.
The default, and 0, mean all available cores.
.It Fl -block Ns = Ns Ar size , Fl -block-size Ns = Ns Ar size
Set the block size, from 64K to 1G.
The default is 16M.
Larger blocks compress better and smaller ones use more threads.
.It Fl -dedup Ns Op = Ns Ar size
Replace repeats of 256 bytes or more, found up to
.Ar size
back, by copy commands.
The default
.Ar size
is 256M and the largest is 64G; it must exceed the block size.
The value must follow
.Sq = .
.It Fl -no-dedup
Do not replace long repeats.
This is the default.
Of
.Fl -dedup
and
.Fl -no-dedup ,
the last one given wins.
.It Fl -memory Ns = Ns Ar size
Set the memory limit.
The default,
.Cm auto ,
is half of physical memory, or of a smaller cgroup limit, or 4G if neither
is known.
Fewer threads are used if the limit requires, and a stream that cannot fit
is refused before anything is allocated.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Report compression statistics on standard error.
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Suppress warnings.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a summary of the options.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Pp
A
.Ar size
is a number of bytes, optionally followed by
.Cm K ,
.Cm M
or
.Cm G
for powers of 1024, in either case, each optionally followed by
.Cm B
or
.Cm iB .
Block and window sizes are rounded up to a power of two.
The value of a long option may follow
.Sq =
or be the next argument, except for
.Fl -dedup .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 4n -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
An error occurred.
.It 141
Standard output was closed before the output was complete.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compress a file, leaving
.Pa notes.txt
and writing
.Pa notes.txt.acz :
.Pp
.Dl acz notes.txt
.Pp
Decompress it:
.Pp
.Dl unacz notes.txt.acz
.Pp
Compress a tar stream on eight threads with long-repeat removal:
.Pp
.Dl tar cf - src | acz -T8 --dedup > src.tar.acz
.Pp
Check a compressed file:
.Pp
.Dl acz -t src.tar.acz
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gzip 1 ,
.Xr xz 1 ,
.Xr zstd 1
.Rs
.%A G. G. Langdon, Jr.
.%T An Introduction to Arithmetic Coding
.%J IBM Journal of Research and Development
.%V 28
.%N 2
.%P 135-149
.%D 1984
.Re
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Pa .acz
format is specified in the documentation of
.Pa acz/src/format.rs .
The format may change before release 1.0.
Each release reads only the format version it writes.
